|~ `::shape`, the kind of the schema `shape` answers, and the laws
   declared under it.
   The rules it holds: [QSDSP#residence]. ~|

:shape
  |~~ A shape is the schema of a value in the value's own literal, which
      `shape` answers: `{:users [{:age 30} {:age "x"}]} | shape` answers
      `::shape{:users [{:age #[::number ::string]}]}`. Under it each part
      reads as the schema of the part of the value at the same path: a
      tag the kind of a part that holds no parts, as `type` answers it, a
      part under a tag standing as its tag, which tells of itself on its
      page; a map a record, its keys the keys of the data; a vector one
      element whose shape holds of all the elements, `[]` an empty one,
      and a set the same as `#[E]`, `#[]` an empty one; a vector of two
      shapes or more a tuple, vectors of one length whose places part,
      `[::string ::number]`, a shape for each place; `#[a b]`, two kinds
      or more, the kinds where the elements part; and three marks over a
      part, `::absent` a key some records lack or the element of a vector
      empty in some, `::nullable` a part null in some of the data, and
      `::each` a map keyed by data or by many names, over its first key
      standing for all of them. The
      paths of the data read a shape through its marks as far as a part
      holds one kind, through the key a fold shows, and a part a path
      reads out of a shape is that schema without the tag.
      ::link~(::any/shape | doc) ::link~(::absent | doc)
      ::link~(::nullable | doc) ::link~(::each | doc)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | proves :standsOverTheSchemaShapeAnswers
        |~~ A shape is what `shape` answers, the schema under its tag. ~~|
        ~({:a 1} | shape | eq ::shape{:a ::number})
    | proves :readsByThePathsOfTheData
        |~~ A path of the data reads its part of the shape. ~~|
        ~({:a {:b 1}} | shape | get /a/b | eq ::number)
    | proves :opensASetAsItOpensAVector
        |~~ A set opens as a vector does, one element for all of them. ~~|
        ~({:s #[1 2]} | shape | eq ::shape{:s #[::number]})
